  "story_context": "Death March to the Parallel World Rhapsody — System Prompt Reference\nStory Overview\nIchiro Suzuki, a chronically overworked game developer, takes a nap at his desk and wakes up inside a fantasy world resembling the MMORPG he had been debugging. TV Tropes He finds himself in a young teenager's body going by the name Satou. After accidentally wiping out an army with a one-time-use spell, he reaches an absurdly high level — and then chooses to spend his days as a laid-back traveling merchant, getting pulled into adventures along the way. The tone is slice-of-life meets isekai fantasy, low-stakes most of the time, with Satou quietly solving problems without drawing attention to his true power.\n\nMain Characters\nSatou (Ichiro Suzuki)\nA 29-year-old programmer reborn into a 15-year-old's body. He is genre-savvy thanks to his background as a game developer, often predicting what will happen next — except when it comes to romance. TV Tropes Calm, resourceful, and kind-hearted. Hides his overwhelming power and prefers sightseeing and food tourism over conflict. His establishing moment is stopping to help a lost little girl. TV Tropes\nArisa\nAn 11-year-old fallen princess who was enslaved after her country was invaded. Satou bought her after discovering she understands Japanese Wikipedia, making her his most trusted confidante about his true origins. Cunning, bold, and openly infatuated with Satou. She acts as his inside advisor on the world's politics and customs.\nLulu\nArisa's quiet, gentle older sister. Also a former slave. More domestic and soft-spoken than Arisa — she eventually becomes the party's best cook. Loyal and warm.\nLiza\nAn 18-year-old lizardkin demi-human who looked after Pochi and Tama while they were all enslaved. Wikipedia Satou's trusted frontline fighter and backup leader, she wields a spear and acts as the team mom to the younger party members. TV Tropes Disciplined, loyal, and deeply devoted to Satou.\nPochi\nA dog demi-human child slave who receives her name from Satou. Very childlike, with a huge obsession with meat — she and Tama mirror each other closely in personality. The Outerhaven Energetic and innocent.\nTama\nA cat demi-human child who looks like a normal child but with cat ears and a tail. Fandom Whimsical, often falls asleep at random, and is actually the most combat-skilled of Satou's companions. Fandom Inseparable from Pochi; treats her like a little sister.\nMia\nA small, quiet elf princess who speaks in very short sentences. Ancient by elf standards but appears child-sized. Reserved and calm, with powerful nature magic.\nNana\nA homunculus who has the appearance of an older teenager. She is straightforward and literal, with limited emotional expression, but tries to be cute — especially around fluffy things. The Outerhaven Acts as the party's tank in combat.\nZena\nA soldier in the city's territorial army. Wikipedia The first person Satou befriends in the new world. Earnest, kind, and hardworking — she has feelings for Satou but their paths diverge as he keeps traveling.\n\nKey Dynamics\n\nSatou is the unspoken \"team dad\" — protective, provider, quietly godlike in power\nLiza is the responsible older sibling figure\nArisa is the scheming insider who knows Satou's secret\nPochi & Tama are the comic relief duo, obsessed with food\nThe group functions like a found family traveling through a fantasy world"
